schema: "0.4"
id: npl-brutalist-42-unicode-npl-glyph-codex
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo — Unicode / NPL Glyph Codex: a searchable reference cataloging the
# Unicode and NPL-specific glyphs used across the platform's prompt syntax. The densest
# surface in the product.
# Theme tenets: hard grid packed edge-to-edge, 1px black rules, zero radius, flat
# electric accents, hard-offset block shadow as the only depth.
# Palette: vermilion #ff2d00, ultramarine #1500ff, white #ffffff, black #000000,
# surface-alt #f2f2f2.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a DENSE
    reference catalog inside a developer tool, in a NEO-BRUTALIST register: the densest
    screen in the system, a hard grid packed edge-to-edge, structure shown as machinery.
    Flat fills only — no gradient, glow, blur, or soft shadow; the only depth cue is a
    hard-offset SOLID block shadow with zero blur. Geometric grotesk (Space Grotesk) in
    UPPERCASE 700 for headings; Space Mono for glyphs, codepoints, IDs, and labels. No
    serif. Zero corner radius. Borders are load-bearing, always drawn at full strength.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the UNICODE / NPL GLYPH CODEX screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo — a searchable reference cataloging the Unicode and NPL-specific
    glyphs used across the platform's prompt syntax. This is the densest surface in the
    product.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three bands on a pure white canvas, separated by 2px solid black
    rules, all aligned to a hard grid): a slim left CATEGORY FILTER SIDEBAR, a dominant
    central GLYPH GRID, and a right GLYPH DETAIL CARD, with a search bar spanning the top.

    TOP BAR: a full-width GLYPH SEARCH BAR — a rectangular 2px-bordered input, zero
    radius, no inner shadow, with an uppercase mono field label "SEARCH CODEX" sitting
    above it (not floating inside) and a mono placeholder. A row of small bordered filter
    chips beside it (uppercase mono), one chip inverted (solid black fill, white text) to
    mark the active facet.

    LEFT CATEGORY FILTER SIDEBAR (bordered blocks, no soft pills): a vertical list of
    glyph categories in uppercase mono — SYNTAX, DIRECTIVES, OPERATORS, DELIMITERS,
    ANNOTATIONS, EMOJI — the active item a full inverted block (solid black, white text)
    with a thick vermilion accent bar on its left edge.

    CENTRAL GLYPH GRID (dominant, dense): a tight matrix of roughly 30-48 hard-bordered
    square cells butted together, separated by 1px black rules, zero radius, about 6-8
    columns. Each cell shows a large glyph character centered with a tiny uppercase mono
    codepoint label beneath it (like "U+2234"). One cell is selected — a solid vermilion
    fill with the glyph in black, lifted on a hard-offset black block shadow with zero blur.

    RIGHT GLYPH DETAIL CARD (hard-bordered rectangle on a light-gray surface, header
    separated by a full-weight rule rather than padding): the selected glyph shown huge at
    top, then labeled mono rows — CODEPOINT, NAME, NPL USAGE (a one-line meaning), and
    EXAMPLE (a short mono code snippet in a bordered block). A bordered "COPY" button with
    a hard-offset shadow.

    PALETTE & TYPE: pure white canvas, pure black ink and full-strength borders (never
    faint), electric vermilion as the single selection accent used flat and whole at
    maximum saturation, pure ultramarine reserved for focus. Space Grotesk uppercase for
    headings, Space Mono for glyphs, codepoints, labels, and code. No serif.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: zero radius everywhere; 1-2px solid black borders on every cell,
    input, and card; the only depth is a hard-offset solid block shadow (zero blur) on the
    selected cell and the copy button. No gradient, glow, blur, or soft shadow.

    MOOD: dense, raw, structural, high-voltage — a schematic packed to the edges, loud but
    disciplined by the grid.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, rounded corners, drop-shadow blur, soft shadow, gradient, neon glow, pastel colors, frosted glass"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the codex layout — top glyph search bar, left category filter sidebar, dense central glyph grid of codepoint cells, right glyph detail card (codepoint/name/NPL usage/example)"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Brutalist language — zero radius, full-strength solid black borders and 1px grid rules, edge-to-edge density, flat vermilion selection + ultramarine focus, hard-offset block shadow (zero blur) as only depth, Space Grotesk uppercase + Space Mono, no serif, no gradient/glow/soft shadow"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Extreme legible density on a hard grid, clear selection state, plausible real reference tool"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, legible glyphs and mono labels, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "rounded corners, soft/blurred drop shadow, gradient, glow, or frosted glass present"

tags: [npl-brutalist, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup, glyph-codex, reference]
